    "text": "Implementation contract (short):\n- Requirement indices -> owning file:\n  - 0-14: game/apple_basket.py (game logic, input, rendering, state).\n  - game/__init__.py: package marker only.\n- State ownership:\n  - Game class in apple_basket.py owns: score (int), missed (int), apples (list of dict{x,y}), basket_pos (x,y), move_dir (int), spawn_timer (float), game_over (bool).\n- Interfaces:\n  - Game.reset() -> None (reinitialize all state).\n  - Game.spawn_apple() -> None (adds an apple dict to apples).\n  - Game.update(dt: float) -> None (advance timers, apples, check collisions).\n  - Game.handle_event(event: pygame.Event) -> None (apply key input; prints controls).\n- Coordinate convention:\n  - Screen origin (0,0) top-left, y increases downward. Basket position is top-left of its image.\n  - Apple represented by center (x,y) and radius.\n- Lifecycle:\n  - init: assets loaded, Game.reset() called.\n  - play: update and draw run each frame while not game_over.\n  - terminal: when missed==3 -> game_over True; apples stop moving/spawning; prints \"GAME OVER\".\n  - reset: pressing 'R' calls reset(), prints \"RESTART\", clears apples, resets counters and resumes.\n  - quit: pressing Escape or window close prints \"QUIT\" and exits.\n\nNow I will write the promised files implementing this contract.",
